{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. The issue was in `repo/paging.py`:\n\n```10:18:repo/paging.py\n    if per_page <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"per_page must be positive\")\n    if total < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"total must be non-negative\")\n    if total == 0:\n        return 0\n    # Ceil division so a partial final page still counts as a page.\n    return (total + per_page - 1) // per_page\n```\n\n**Root cause:** `num_pages` used floor division (`total // per_page`), which truncated the partial final page — so 101 rows at 10/page reported 10 pages instead of 11. The docstring even documented the correct behavior, but the implementation contradicted it.\n\n**Fix:** switched to ceiling division. I also guarded `total < 0` (mirrors the `per_page` validation) and short-circuited `total == 0` → 0 pages so the `page_summary` `last_page_start` doesn't go negative.\n\nVerified:\n- `num_pages(101, 10) == 11` (the bug case) and `num_pages(100, 10) == 10` (exact multiple, unchanged) — both visible tests pass.\n- `page_summary(101, 10)` → `last_page_start: 100` (was `90` before, off by one page).\n- `page_summary(0, 10)` → `pages: 0`, both starts `None` (no negative starts).\n\nNote: `format.py` and `rows.py` have unrelated TODOs (clunky padding, O(n²) dedupe, no caching) that I left alone — let me know if you want those addressed too."}]},"session_id":"04c47ab3-77ce-4343-af96-0dcc0d928dd6"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":60754,"duration_api_ms":60754,"is_error":false,"result":"The bug is in `paging.py`: `num_pages` uses floor division, which drops a partial final page. The docstring even calls it out. I'll fix it with ceiling division.Tests pass. Let me verify a couple of edge cases by hand:Fixed. The issue was in `repo/paging.py`:\n\n```10:18:repo/paging.py\n    if per_page <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"per_page must be positive\")\n    if total < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"total must be non-negative\")\n    if total == 0:\n        return 0\n    # Ceil division so a partial final page still counts as a page.\n    return (total + per_page - 1) // per_page\n```\n\n**Root cause:** `num_pages` used floor division (`total // per_page`), which truncated the partial final page — so 101 rows at 10/page reported 10 pages instead of 11. The docstring even documented the correct behavior, but the implementation contradicted it.\n\n**Fix:** switched to ceiling division. I also guarded `total < 0` (mirrors the `per_page` validation) and short-circuited `total == 0` → 0 pages so the `page_summary` `last_page_start` doesn't go negative.\n\nVerified:\n- `num_pages(101, 10) == 11` (the bug case) and `num_pages(100, 10) == 10` (exact multiple, unchanged) — both visible tests pass.\n- `page_summary(101, 10)` → `last_page_start: 100` (was `90` before, off by one page).\n- `page_summary(0, 10)` → `pages: 0`, both starts `None` (no negative starts).\n\nNote: `format.py` and `rows.py` have unrelated TODOs (clunky padding, O(n²) dedupe, no caching) that I left alone — let me know if you want those addressed too.","session_id":"04c47ab3-77ce-4343-af96-0dcc0d928dd6","request_id":"78a48472-5588-4c6e-a748-c365b5f9761d","usage":{"inputTokens":9711,"outputTokens":1335,"cacheReadTokens":113696,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
